raw_model_text:
Looking at the timer observations, the core issue is clear:
- `weld-time-4` (clock=5000ms): poweruptimer.Q=true → correct for 5s elapsed
- `weld-time-5` (clock=5749ms): poweruptimer.Q=false, ET=0 → **incorrect** - should still be in normal mode (InNormalMode should remain true)

The bug: `PowerUpTimer(IN := NOT PowerUpTimer.Q, ...)` resets the timer after it completes. When Q becomes true, IN becomes false, which resets Q to false on the next scan. This causes oscillation between inhibit and normal mode states instead of latching to normal mode after 5s.

Fix: Add an `InNormalMode` latch that transitions from false→true when power-up timer completes, and remains true until E-stop resets it.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"VAR
    // Power-up initialization timer: 5-second inhibit period
    PowerUpTimer: TON;
    // Gap signal debounce timer during normal monitoring
    DebounceTimer: TON;
END_VAR", "new":"VAR
    // Power-up initialization timer: 5-second inhibit period
    PowerUpTimer: TON;
    // Gap signal debounce timer during normal monitoring
    DebounceTimer: TON;
    // Latch to persist normal monitoring state after power-up timer completes
    InNormalMode: BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR"}, {"old":"    // E-stop inactive (Weld_E_Stop_NC = TRUE): normal/state logic

    // Power-up timer: runs for 5s, gated by E-stop (already TRUE here)
    PowerUpTimer(IN := NOT PowerUpTimer.Q, PT := T#5s);

    // Determine current operating phase
    IF NOT PowerUpTimer.Q THEN", "new":"    // E-stop inactive (Weld_E_Stop_NC = TRUE): normal/state logic

    // Power-up timer: runs for 5s, gated by E-stop (already TRUE here)
    // Only enable timer while still in initialization phase
    PowerUpTimer(IN := NOT InNormalMode, PT := T#5s);

    // Latch to normal mode when power-up timer completes (first time only)
    // This prevents oscillation where timer Q resets immediately after completion
    IF PowerUpTimer.Q AND NOT InNormalMode THEN
        InNormalMode := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    // Determine current operating phase
    IF NOT InNormalMode THEN"}]}
```
